  "notes": "B.A. Accounting, College of Business and Economics. QUARTER SYSTEM — all credits are quarter hours. Built from the official WWU catalog program page (https://catalog.wwu.edu/preview_program.php?catoid=21&poid=9987, 'Accounting, BA', 2024-2025 catalog) and the CBE accounting requirements (https://cbe.wwu.edu/files/2021-11/BoS%20Acctg_MIS%20Conc.pdf). Foundation 30cr (MATH 157, DSCI 205, ECON 206/207, ACCT 240/245, MGMT 271, MIS 220); Business Core 24cr (DSCI 305, MGMT 311, MIS 320, FIN 341, OPS 360, MKTG 380); Accounting courses 48cr: ACCT 341/342/343 (Intermediate I/II/III), ACCT 321 (AIS I), ACCT 331 (Cost Management), ACCT 375 (Taxation), ACCT 441 (Advanced Financial), ACCT 461 (Auditing), ACCT 470 (Commercial Law), ACCT 490 (Internship), plus 8cr of 400-level accounting electives (excludes 441/461/470/490). Note: the catalog header lists '100 credits' but the specified course requirements total 102 quarter credits; this plan reflects the actual requirements. GURs modeled as choice slots. 180 quarter credits total (102 major + 42 GUR + 36 electives).",
